From a545209c66c61780832f8551f3db95307b81774f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Veron Williams <magnusboysacct@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 10:33:44 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Contact-scoped client portal access (backend) + per-user
 password hashing

Adds a second kind of portal login tied to one client contact. It sees only
the projects assigned to that contact (projects.contact_id), re-checked live
on every call. The client-level (manager) login is unchanged.

- Migration 20260936000000: contact_id on client_portal_sessions;
  client_contact_portal_access (no browser grants); _portal_session_ctx and
  _portal_can_see_project helpers; _portal_session_client now manager-only,
  so invoices, contracts, estimates, change-order approval and reviews are
  closed to contacts without further changes; contact-aware get_portal_data,
  get_portal_comments, insert_portal_comment, log_portal_event; staff RPCs to
  invite, check and revoke a project's contact.
- Contract edge functions refuse contact sessions.
- client-portal-login / client-password-reset: PBKDF2-SHA256 with per-user
  salt (legacy shared-salt hashes upgraded on next login), contact
  setup/login/reset, strict email validation (closes a PostgREST .or()
  filter injection in the email lookups).
- supabase/tests/portal-access: local-Postgres harness; manager outputs
  identical before/after; 71 leakage tests; 21 password tests.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DpyMC7wNSLZyjCRiSGNmSu
